cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the article and release v1.0.0 of this repository."
title: "Analysis code for: Accuracy of robotic full-crown preparation and preoperative crown fit"
abstract: >-
  Python analysis code for an in vitro study of robot-assisted full-crown preparation and
  the seating fit of preoperatively fabricated crowns. The repository contains (i) the
  Geomagic Wrap Python scripts that segment the ideal preparation and the scanned models
  into seven anatomical regions, register the seating and crown scans, extract the
  shoulder-margin contours and export the meshes to STL; and (ii) the standalone Python
  scripts that compute the per-specimen print-scan-registration (PSR) correction,
  preparation accuracy, crown printing accuracy, internal fit and marginal gap, together
  with the validation of the semi-automated region segmentation. The two sets are kept in
  separate top-level directories, 01_geomagic_wrap_scripts/ and 02_python_analysis/.
